\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
If a connected closed smooth Riemannian manifold of positive dimension has injectivity radius equal to diameter, must some positive scaling of its metric be isometric to a standard round sphere, real/complex/quaternionic projective space, or Cayley plane?

\subsection{Short English statement}
If a connected closed smooth Riemannian manifold of positive dimension has injectivity radius equal to diameter, must some positive scaling of its metric be isometric to a standard round sphere, real/complex/quaternionic projective space, or Cayley plane?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/The-metric-Blaschke-theorem-September-23-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

